WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.970
Jean-Luc Picard is one of Star Trek's most
legendary captains, but the man has a long,

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.630
complicated history with the Enterprise and
its crew.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:13.950
If you want the lowdown on his story, then
here’s Picard’s entire timeline explained.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.510
Born in La Barre, France, young Jean-Luc Picard
had a troubled upbringing.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.640
The first glimpse of his childhood comes in
the "Star Trek: The Next Generation" episode

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.609
titled "Family," where he visits his brother
Robert on Earth.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.609
In this episode, we learn that Jean-Luc and
Robert helped their father take care of the

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:32.000
family's vineyards.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.020
We also learn that the rest of Jean-Luc's
family are traditionalists.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.140
They don't trust advanced technology like
replicators and certainly don't have a high

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.450
opinion of the vaunted Starfleet.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.910
All the while, his brother is something of
a bully to him.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.020
But we learn much more about the young Picard's
early life in Season 2 of "Star Trek: Picard."

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.270
Apparently, he had an especially close relationship
with his mother Yvette.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:58.301
But Yvette suffered from severe mental illness,
and despite her husband Maurice's pleas, she

00:00:58.301 --> 00:01:00.030
refused to seek help.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.770
As a result, Maurice is often forced to lock
her in her room to prevent her from self-harm

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.630
during particularly difficult episodes.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.240
This leads to one of the most life-altering
moments in Jean-Luc's life.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.259
Amid one of his mother's episodes, she calls
out to Jean-Luc to let her out of her room.

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:19.070
When he does, it leads to his mother's suicide.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:23.040
Picard carries the guilt of this incident
with him all of his life, only finally coming

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.066
to terms with it as an older man.

00:01:25.332 --> 00:01:30.270
Moving past the tragedy, Jean-Luc's time on
the family vineyard continues to frustrate

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.720
him, as he has little interest in the family
business of winemaking.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.810
It doesn't take long for Jean-Luc to figure
out that his path leads to the stars, and

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.090
the future Enterprise captain soon gains a
reputation as an overachiever, becoming a

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.369
sports champion as well as valedictorian of
his high school.

00:01:45.369 --> 00:01:53.076
"Never sought president of the school, valedictorian,
athletic hero with your arms raised in victory?"

00:01:53.076 --> 00:01:57.250
Against his father's wishes, Jean-Luc leaves
home for Starfleet Academy as soon as the

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:02.210
opportunity arises, though it takes him two
attempts before his application is accepted.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:06.420
In Season 6's "Tapestry," we learn a little
bit more about what kind of man he is during

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.759
his Academy days.

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:13.291
Far from the steady, stoic, commanding leader,
Picard is a brash, fiery, cavalier sort, and

00:02:13.291 --> 00:02:16.810
even something of a womanizer while at Starfleet
Academy.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:21.951
It's there that he meets both Jack Crusher
and Beverly Howard, and they become close friends.

00:02:21.951 --> 00:02:27.519
We also learn that he had something of an
unrequited crush on Academy mate Marta Batanides.

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:31.470
But we also witnessed an event just after
his exit from the Academy that leaves its

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.100
deepest mark on him.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:37.100
While waiting for his first assignments, Picard
gets into a brawl with a group of Nausicaans

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.769
over a game of dom-jot.

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:42.750
Overmatched but refusing to back down, Picard
is stabbed through the heart, and while he

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.292
survives the injury, he's left with an artificial
organ in his heart's place.

00:02:47.728 --> 00:02:51.580
We don't have many details about Picard's
Picard's post-Academy life before he got command

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.626
of his own ship.

00:02:52.626 --> 00:02:56.740
We learn in the second season TNG episode
"The Measure of a Man" that he once served

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.980
aboard the USS Reliant, but more is known
about his time aboard the USS Stargazer.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.960
There, Picard started as a bridge officer,
but he made his way up the ranks the old-fashioned

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.050
way — being the highest ranked officer left
alive in the middle of a battle.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:15.489
Jean-Luc commanded the Stargazer for two decades,
until he and the surviving crew were forced

00:03:15.489 --> 00:03:19.409
to abandon the vessel after a battle with
a Ferengi ship.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:21.145
"Who are they?

00:03:21.145 --> 00:03:22.145
Identify them."

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:25.629
"They're turning for a third pass at us, sir!

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:27.849
We can't take another hit, Captain!"

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:32.440
That final battle led to the "Picard Maneuver"
being coined for the unorthodox move Jean-Luc

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.960
made to destroy the enemy vessel.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.810
More personally relevant to Picard was his
friendship with Jack Crusher aboard the Stargazer.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:44.620
Jack was the late husband of Beverly Crusher
and father to Wesley, both of whom wind up

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.489
serving aboard the Enterprise.

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:50.880
It's Picard who, while commanding the Stargazer,
sent Jack Crusher on an away mission that

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.160
led to his death.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:57.159
When we meet Picard in the Next Generation
series premiere, he's already taken command

00:03:57.159 --> 00:03:58.500
of his famous ship.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.599
His orders send him to Deneb IV:

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:06.420
"Beyond which lies the great, unexplored mass
of the galaxy."

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:11.349
On the way there, the Enterprise has its first
fateful meeting with the trickster, god-like

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:12.349
alien Q.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:16.389
With a few short breaks here and there, Picard
remains in command of the Enterprise-D until

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:19.620
its destruction in 1994's Star Trek: Generations.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:24.630
He and his stalwart crew get to explore quite
a bit of that "great, unexplored mass," and

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:30.270
along the way, they encounter aliens both
benevolent and hostile, including the fan-favorite Borg.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:35.940
In the season two episode "Q-Who?," the deceitful
Q uses his powers to send the Enterprise deep

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.570
into unexplored parts of the galaxy where
they encounter the Borg for the first time.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:45.570
The Borg act as a single collective mind and
rebuff all attempts at communication in favor

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.250
of seeking to overpower the Enterprise.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.220
Although they're eventually returned to Federation
space, it's clear the crew hasn't seen the

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.565
last of the Borg.

00:04:53.565 --> 00:04:56.284
"Since they're aware of your existence…"

00:05:00.378 --> 00:05:02.220
"They will be coming."

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.700
The Borg re-emerge in the two-parter "The
Best of Both Worlds," when they kidnap Picard

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.259
and assimilate him into their collective.

00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:12.990
Picard is eventually rescued, and it proves
the Borg's Achilles' heel as his connection

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:16.539
to the collective allows Data to command the
invaders to sleep.

00:05:16.539 --> 00:05:20.320
But it's clear Picard is severely traumatized
by the experience.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.569
This wouldn't be Picard's last encounter with
the Borg, however.

00:05:23.569 --> 00:05:28.783
In "I, Borg," the Enterprise crew rescue a
Borg who's somehow capable of independent thought.

00:05:28.783 --> 00:05:33.270
They meet him again in the two-part "Descent"
as the leader of a group of liberated Borg

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.680
resisting the control of Data's twin brother,
Lore.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:40.630
And finally, Picard would be forced to confront
the Borg and his overwhelming need for vengeance

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:45.910
against them in 1996's Star Trek: First Contact,
when the aliens attempt to assimilate the

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:49.607
Federation by going back in time before the
Federation's founding.

00:05:50.091 --> 00:05:54.350
One of the most interesting relationships
on Star Trek: The Next Generation is the kinship

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.550
that develops between Picard and the android
Data.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.560
By the end of the series and the subsequent
films, it's clear Picard holds the android

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:02.780
close to his heart.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.780
He sees Data as, at the very least, a close
friend.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:09.400
However, at times their connection doesn't
seem all that different than that between

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.030
a father and a son.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:15.220
Picard reveals part of his fascination with,
and admiration for, Data in the second season

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.910
episode "The Measure of a Man."

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:21.530
Data attempts to resign his commission so
that an insistent Starfleet scientist can't

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:24.460
run experiments on him which will wipe out
his memory.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:29.000
The scientist argues Data, as a machine, doesn't
have the right to resign his commission, and

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.350
Picard assumes the difficult task of proving
that Data is a sentient being with the right

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:37.680
to make his own choices and not be subjected
to anyone else's ownership.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.030
Picard famously tells the presiding judge:

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:43.930
"Your Honor, Starfleet was founded to seek
out new life.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.680
Well, there it sits."

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:50.020
Data is tragically forced to sacrifice himself
at the end of the final Next Generation film,

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:52.590
2002's Star Trek: Nemesis, though it's hinted
he could return in a new form.

00:06:52.868 --> 00:06:58.120
When Picard is appointed as "arbiter of succession"
by the dying Klingon chancellor K'mpec, he

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:00.740
helps alter the course of the Klingon Empire.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:05.940
As arbiter, Picard's job is to weigh the worth
of the two challengers, Gowron and Duras.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:11.438
By the end of season four's "Reunion," K'mpec
is dead, and no new chancellor has been officially announced.

00:07:11.438 --> 00:07:15.620
Things get even more complicated when Worf,
claiming vengeance for the death of his mate

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.990
K'Ehleyr at Duras' hands, transports over
to Duras' ship and kills him.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:23.870
Picard finally announces Gowron as the rightful
chancellor.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:28.300
But two Klingon sisters from the House of
Duras appear with a boy named Toral, who they

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:33.210
claim is the son of Duras and should therefore
be considered a challenger in the rite.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:37.770
Picard later confirms Toral is the son of
Duras, but that he is too young and inexperienced

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.610
to be considered chancellor.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.990
The decision pushes the Klingon Empire into
open civil war.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:47.850
Eventually, the House of Duras' conspiracy
with the Romulans is exposed, and Gowron presides

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.604
over a reunited empire.

00:07:49.604 --> 00:07:53.835
As an added benefit, Worf and his house are
redeemed in the eyes of his people.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:58.271
In spite of their respective series being
separated by two decades, Jean-Luc Picard

00:07:58.271 --> 00:08:01.450
proves to be an important figure in the life
of Spock.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:06.280
The first time Picard significantly touches
Spock's life is in the third season's "Sarek."

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.660
Spock himself doesn't appear, but his father
Sarek boards the Enterprise to negotiate a

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:13.000
trade deal with the Legarans.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:17.770
Unfortunately, it soon becomes clear that
Sarek suffers from a rare degenerative disorder

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:20.509
that causes his emotions to run wild.

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:24.680
Picard agrees to a mind meld, so that Sarek
can maintain enough control to continue with

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.039
the negotiations.

00:08:26.039 --> 00:08:29.755
"My mind to your mind."

00:08:29.755 --> 00:08:33.729
In the two-part "Unification," Picard comes
face-to-face with Spock himself.

00:08:33.729 --> 00:08:38.570
He's sent to Romulus to find Spock because
Starfleet fears the Vulcan may have defected

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:39.849
to their rivals.

00:08:39.849 --> 00:08:44.800
Instead, Picard learns Spock is involved in
secret negotiations with the hopes of bringing

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.440
the Vulcan and Romulan people back together.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:51.540
By the end of the two-parter, Sarek finally
succumbs to his illness, and "Unification"

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:55.250
ends with a compassionate and tender gesture
on Picard's part.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:59.140
He allows Spock to mind meld with him, so
that Spock may connect with the parts of his

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.594
father that Picard had experienced.

00:09:01.758 --> 00:09:07.310
Of all the Star Trek series of the past six
decades, none can boast as inventive or satisfying

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:11.820
a finale as "All Good Things…," the final
episode of The Next Generation.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:15.900
Q causes Picard to jump both backwards and
forwards in time, so that the story takes

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.920
place in the present, past, and decades in
the future, where Picard is an older man suffering

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.410
from a degenerative mental disease.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.510
Picard's trips to the future are particularly
difficult.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:32.040
With future versions of Beverly Crusher, Data,
and Geordi La Forge all aware of his condition,

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:35.940
it makes it that much more challenging to
convince anyone in that time that he actually

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:38.555
is experiencing what he says he's experiencing.

00:09:38.781 --> 00:09:40.401
"Yes, yes, I know what you're thinking.

00:09:40.401 --> 00:09:41.750
It's the Irumodic Syndrome.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:44.519
He's beginning to lose his mind, the old man.

00:09:44.519 --> 00:09:45.519
Well, it's not that.

00:09:45.519 --> 00:09:46.990
And I'm not daydreaming either."

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:51.160
None of the TNG movies hinted towards the
illness beginning to emerge, and the future

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.761
of the episode was only one possible timeline.

00:09:54.139 --> 00:09:58.769
When the Next Generation crew gets on the
big screen for the first time in 1994's Star

00:09:58.769 --> 00:10:02.970
Trek: Generations, it sadly comes with the
death of William Shatner's Captain Kirk.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:07.620
And unfortunately, Jean-Luc Picard suffers
some much more personal losses, both in the

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.700
beginning and at the end of the game-changing
film.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:15.580
Early in Generations, the Enterprise's empathic
counselor Deanna Troi senses something is

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:20.680
terribly wrong, and when she finds Captain
Picard flipping through a photo album, Jean-Luc

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:25.580
reveals he's just received news that his brother
Robert and his son have been killed in a fire.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:30.490
The usually stoic Picard laments the loss
of his beloved nephew and reflects that without

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:35.029
a wife or children of his own, he'll be the
last one in his family line.

00:10:35.029 --> 00:10:39.940
"I've come to feel that Rene was as close
as I would get to having a child of my own."

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:43.180
By the end of the movie, Picard loses the
Enterprise itself.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:47.810
The ship barely survives a battle with a Klingon
Bird of Prey run by the villainous sisters

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:49.370
Lursa and B'Etor.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:55.210
The crew evacuates to the ship's saucer section,
which crashes on the surface of Veridian III.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:11:01.160
Thankfully, as Picard predicts, the Enterprise-D
won't be the last ship to carry the name Enterprise.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:06.500
The final big screen appearance of Jean-Luc
Picard comes with 2002's Star Trek: Nemesis.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:11.240
The Enterprise is sent to Romulus to meet
the Romulan Empire's new leader, who we soon

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.890
learn has an unexpected connection to Picard.

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:17.620
As it turns out, Praetor Shinzon is a clone
of Jean-Luc.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:21.870
The Romulans cloned the captain in hopes of
one day replacing him with their own identical

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:26.210
agent, but when one of the empire's many power
shifts took place, the clone was sent to a

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:29.410
labor colony with the enslaved people of Remus.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:34.180
Shinzon lures Picard to Romulus because the
cloning process that created him is now killing

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:38.850
him, and his only potential cure is a complete
blood transfusion with Picard.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:42.760
Ultimately, Shinzon's plans to kill Picard
and destroy the Federation are foiled, and

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.750
the clone villain dies fighting his older
counterpart.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:50.250
On top of all that, Nemesis includes huge
shifts in Picard's life, including the loss

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.220
of Riker as his "number one."

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:57.210
We learn early in the film that Riker is finally
taking the captain's chair on the USS Titan,

00:11:57.210 --> 00:12:00.060
and his new wife, Deanna Troi, is coming with
him.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:04.250
Picard means for Data to replace Riker as
his first officer, but the android sacrifices

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:07.149
himself to save his friends in the final battle.

00:12:07.359 --> 00:12:12.940
In anticipation of Star Trek: Picard, IDW
released the prequel mini-series Star Trek:

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:13.940
Picard — Countdown.

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:18.630
The story takes place six years after the
events of Nemesis and 14 years before Picard.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.320
Picard is an admiral commanding the USS Verity.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:26.839
Romulus' star is close to going supernova,
and the Romulan Empire abandons some of its

00:12:26.839 --> 00:12:30.370
usual paranoia and secrecy for Starfleet's
help.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:35.490
Unfortunately, complications arise when Picard
travels to the Romulan colony of Yuyat Beta.

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:39.800
The Romulans there have enslaved the native
population and neglected to tell Starfleet

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:43.220
because, in the words of one of the colony's
Romulan leaders:

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:47.570
"Evacuating them would be as ridiculous as
evacuating the rocks and trees."

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:51.899
When Picard refuses to relocate the Romulans
without the natives, the colony's leaders

00:12:51.899 --> 00:12:54.570
take him and his first officer prisoner.

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:59.330
Countdown gives us a chance to see Raffi Musiker
— the irreverent first officer who insists

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:06.000
on referring to Picard as "JL" — in action
as Picard's second-in-command during the Romulan evacuation.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:10.949
We also meet the Romulans Zhaban and Laris
while they're still Tal Shiar agents, and

00:13:10.949 --> 00:13:15.060
it's revealed exactly how they eventually
come to work for and live with Picard.

00:13:15.298 --> 00:13:19.899
After the events of "Countdown" are resolved,
Picard and Raffi prepare to scramble a massive

00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:23.830
fleet to relocate the population of the twin
Romulan home worlds.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:29.855
The fleet is assembled at the Utopia Planitia
Shipyards with a workforce of mostly android Synths.

00:13:29.855 --> 00:13:35.230
In a shocking turn of events, however, a plot
masterminded by a Romulan splinter group orchestrates

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.850
a Synth uprising in a historical attack on
Mars.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:42.079
The assault destroys the entire Romulan Rescue
Armada.

00:13:42.079 --> 00:13:46.540
Picard does manage to get some Romulan refugees
moved to the planet Vashti.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:51.410
However, the destruction of the fleet leaves
his relocation plan in tatters and results

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.750
in a ban on synthetic lifeforms.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:58.876
Desperate to fulfill his promise to rescue
the Romulan people, Picard makes a plea to Starfleet.

00:13:58.876 --> 00:14:04.670
He wants to assemble a fleet of formerly mothballed
ships and threatens to resign if they refuse.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:08.209
But In a shocking twist, Starfleet command
accepts his resignation.

00:14:08.209 --> 00:14:13.639
Haunted by his failures and unable to muster
the same kind of respect he had in his prime,

00:14:13.639 --> 00:14:17.420
Picard leaves Starfleet behind and goes into
seclusion at his vineyard.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:21.750
He relocates a number of Romulan refugees
to his home, including his Romulan friends

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.460
Laris and Zhaban.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.970
Trekkies were surprised w hen they tuned in
to "Picard" for the first time.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:32.850
Instead of the bold, commanding captain they
recalled from TNG, they saw a dreary, tired

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:33.970
old man.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:39.053
Following his failure to save Romulus, Picard
spends more than a decade living a solitary life.

00:14:39.053 --> 00:14:44.260
He has only infrequent visits with old friends
from his days on the Enterprise and the Stargazer.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:49.320
But his quiet life in France is upended by
the arrival of a young woman named Dahj.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:53.660
This visitor appears to be the offspring of
his old friend Data, and she's being hunted

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.700
by mysterious unknown forces.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.700
"...everything inside of me says that I'm
safe with you."

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:04.380
As it turns out, Dahj is actually a synthetic
life form, and she may be the key to stopping

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.389
an emerging galactic threat.

00:15:06.389 --> 00:15:10.630
Without the clout he had in his heyday, Picard
is forced to recruit a new crew.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:16.490
This includes Dr. Agnes Jurati, rogue pilot
Cristóbal Rios, a young Romulan monk named

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:18.420
Elnor, and his old friend Raffi.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:23.160
They take on a mission to unravel a conspiracy
and stop a cosmic cataclysm.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:27.500
After several detours, he finally finds the
destination of Dahj's twin sister.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.990
She's working at the Borg Reclamation Project.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:34.180
There, Picard is reunited with the former
Borg drone named Hugh, who's taken it upon

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:37.970
himself to assist other Borg to regain their
former lives.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:42.000
More than just another chance to play hero,
Picard's mission also allows him to finally

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.495
come to terms with the death of Commander
Data.

00:15:44.902 --> 00:15:48.750
While the story in Season 1 of "Star Trek:
Picard" is kicked off by the discovery of

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:53.459
Data's daughter, the action is propelled by
a mystery involving the Synths and a threat

00:15:53.459 --> 00:15:56.150
that could wipe out all life in the galaxy.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:16:00.740
From his Romulan housekeepers, Picard learns
that the threat may involve the Zhat Vash.

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:06.021
To get to the bottom of the conspiracy, Picard
and the crew of Captain Rios' La Sirena must

00:16:06.021 --> 00:16:08.550
track down the scientist Bruce Maddox.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:13.310
The mission is completely unsanctioned, and
it makes Picard a rogue agent in an unlikely

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:14.710
role reversal.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:19.759
During the mission, Picard meets Dahj's twin
sister Soji and is reunited with old friends

00:16:19.759 --> 00:16:24.000
Will Riker and Deanna Troi for the first time
in many years.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.519
They help get him information regarding a
planet called Coppelius.

00:16:27.519 --> 00:16:32.410
It's there that a new race of synthetic lifeforms
is being created, which the Zhat Vash believe

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.300
poses an existential threat to the galaxy.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.839
As the planet comes under attack from a Romulan
fleet, Picard gets assistance from Riker,

00:16:39.839 --> 00:16:42.330
who commands a Federation fleet to stop them.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:47.370
In the aftermath, Picard successfully convinces
Starfleet to lift the ban on synthetic life,

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:50.658
allowing Soji and others like them to live
in peace.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:55.310
The end of the first season of "Picard" includes
a life-altering change in the story of the

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:57.139
former captain of the Enterprise.

00:16:57.139 --> 00:17:01.399
In the aftermath of the Romulan-Federation
clash in the skies above Coppelius, Picard

00:17:01.399 --> 00:17:05.929
finally succumbs to the apparent Irumodic
Syndrome that has long-plagued him, and he

00:17:05.929 --> 00:17:08.010
dies surrounded by his new crew.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:11.789
But on Coppelius, Picard gets a second chance
at life.

00:17:11.789 --> 00:17:17.030
Also on Coppelius is Data's human "brother,"
Altan Soong, who has created a bio-organic

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.329
"golem" body.

00:17:18.329 --> 00:17:22.520
With the help of Jurati, Soong is able to
transfer Picard's consciousness in this new

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:25.720
golem, which is given the form of Picard's
old body.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:29.900
Before the transfer completes though, Picard's
mind is transferred into a simulation module

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.299
where the consciousness of Data also resides.

00:17:32.299 --> 00:17:36.420
As Picard and Data speak, Picard's old friend
makes one final request.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:43.580
"When you leave, I would be profoundly grateful
if you terminated my consciousness."

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:48.429
Resurrected in his new body, Picard enters
the simulation again and says a tearful goodbye

00:17:48.429 --> 00:17:51.950
as he shuts down Data's program one final
time.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:56.450
In his new body, Jean-Luc Picard still has
the form of an elderly man but is free of

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.049
his Irumodic Syndrome.

00:17:58.049 --> 00:18:02.700
Healthy enough to live decades more, he sets
out with a renewed spirit and returns to active

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.200
Starfleet duty.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:08.951
He's accepted back into the service and appointed
to the role of Chancellor of Starfleet Academy.

00:18:09.068 --> 00:18:13.780
As Season 2 of "Picard" begins, Jean-Luc's
life has begun to settle down again, but an

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:16.260
old rival shows up to make trouble.

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:20.880
It turns out to be the not-so-immortal Q in
Season 2 of "Star Trek: Picard."

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.540
Much like he has in the past, Q arrives to
teach Picard a valuable life lesson, and he

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:30.070
does it by throwing Picard and his new crew
into an alternate timeline where Starfleet

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:35.330
is a fascist dictatorship and Picard is their
iron-fisted tyrant ruler.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:42.130
"Through a mirror darkly, and here the man
who holds the glass is darker still."

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:46.650
In this twisted reality, the Federation is
known as the Confederation, and Picard has

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:48.890
defeated all of its greatest enemies.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:53.710
This includes luminaries from "Star Trek"
including Klingon General Martok, Cardassian

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:58.610
Gul Dukat, even beheading Sarek, Director
of the Vulcan Science Academy.

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.169
Picard has to travel back in time to save
the future.

00:19:01.169 --> 00:19:05.730
To solve the mystery of altered existence,
Picard needs the help of the Borg Queen.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:10.130
He also has to come face to face with his
own history when he meets Renée Picard.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:14.390
She's an ancestor of Jean-Luc's who also plays
a key role in the history of space exploration

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:15.978
in the 21st century.

00:19:15.978 --> 00:19:20.703
Her mission to Europa is critical to ensuring
the Federation's future.

00:19:20.703 --> 00:19:25.890
Season 3 of "Star Trek: Picard" was heavily
promoted as the reunion of the crew of the

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:30.636
Enterprise-D, and it's because of an emerging
threat from one of the Federation's most deadly foes.

00:19:30.636 --> 00:19:35.450
After using the USS Titan to come to the rescue
of his dear friend and on-again-off-again

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:40.710
lover Beverly Crusher, Picard uncovers a conspiracy
to infiltrate the Federation.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:45.270
The threads begin to unravel as they encounter
a mercenary pirate named Vadic.

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:49.390
She is one of the leaders of the conspiracy,
and the first foe Picard and his allies have

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:52.450
to defeat in order to bring an end to the
emerging threat.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:56.890
Vadic is a rogue Changeling who spent much
of her life as a prisoner and was tortured

00:19:56.890 --> 00:20:00.309
by Section 31 following the end of the Dominion
War.

00:20:00.309 --> 00:20:03.700
She's bent on revenge and needs Picard's son
to achieve it.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:08.530
With the help of the Titan's jaded captain
Liam Shaw and his first officer Seven of Nine,

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:10.280
they help keep his son safe.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:13.469
But the reasons for the pursuit remain unclear.

00:20:13.469 --> 00:20:18.200
Season 3 of "Star Trek: Picard" introduces
Jack Crusher, the son of Jean-Luc Picard and

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:22.650
Beverly Crusher, whose discovery forever alters
Jean-Luc Picard's life.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:27.190
He is the product of a whirlwind romance following
the events of "Star Trek: Nemesis."

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:31.549
Dr. Crusher hid him from Picard because she
feared he might become the target of his father's

00:20:31.549 --> 00:20:32.940
worst enemies.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:37.120
To keep him a secret, Dr. Crusher cut off
all contact with Jean-Luc and the rest of

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.160
her old Enterprise shipmates.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:43.059
Alongside his mother, Jack grew up on the
edges of the Federation frontier, helping

00:20:43.059 --> 00:20:45.850
to provide aid and supplies to those in need.

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:50.179
But they came under attack from what would
later be revealed to be enemy Changeling agents,

00:20:50.179 --> 00:20:53.020
and they were forced to go to Jean-Luc for
help.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:57.270
Picard is heartbroken that he had been denied
the opportunity to be a father for more than

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.270
20 years.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:06.169
"And you never thought, if you had told me,
it all might have been different."

00:21:06.169 --> 00:21:11.155
Despite the years of secrecy, Picard helps
keep Dr. Crusher and Jack safe from their pursuers.

00:21:11.155 --> 00:21:16.730
With the aid of Riker, Picard hijacks the
USS Titan to do it and exposes the Changeling plot.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:21.500
Ultimately, it's revealed that Jack inherited
a part of Jean-Luc's Borg-assimilated biology.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:25.679
The Changeling, Vadic, was working with the
Borg Queen to use Jack as part of a plan to

00:21:25.679 --> 00:21:27.710
assimilate and destroy the Federation.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:33.460
As Vox, Jack controls the newly created Borg
drones and almost destroys Earth.

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:37.880
But after Picard makes a heartfelt plea to
his son within the Borg collective unconscious,

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.659
Jack rejects the Queen and the pair thwart
her diabolical plans.

